WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.520
- So I heard you met Prince

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.580
and we have this thing on this show.

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.350
Everybody has a Prince story.

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:07.032
I don't, but everybody else does.

00:00:07.032 --> 00:00:10.660
And, I wanna know, what
was your experience?

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:13.740
- My Prince story is that I got a meeting

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:15.660
like a general meeting that
goes meet with this director

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:16.550
and they said, "And Prince."

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:17.730
And I thought like Prince Johnson

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.602
from Santa Monica or something.

00:00:19.602 --> 00:00:20.435
(audience laughing)
- oh, you didn't know

00:00:20.435 --> 00:00:21.520
it was actually prince
that you were seeing?

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.587
- I had no idea.
- Oh, that makes me sweat.

00:00:23.587 --> 00:00:25.050
- Me too.
- Yeah.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:25.883
- Even now.

00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:27.560
And so I rescheduled the meeting twice,

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:28.730
'cause I had a bunch of stuff going on.

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:29.563
They were like are you gonna-

00:00:29.563 --> 00:00:31.107
- You reschedule on Prince.
- You schedule on Prince?

00:00:31.107 --> 00:00:32.810
- I know.
(audience laugh)

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:33.797
So the last time they were like,

00:00:33.797 --> 00:00:34.800
"You're either coming or you're not."

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:35.940
And I was like, "Okay, I'm coming."

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:37.230
- [Kelly] Oh my god.
So then I come

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:38.630
to this meeting at this house

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:40.397
and as soon as I get on the
elevator, that's in the house.

00:00:40.397 --> 00:00:42.870
I'm like, "What is an
elevator in a house?"

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:45.620
The doors open and it's
crush purple velvet.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.710
And I'm like, "Wait, wait,
wait, wait, wait, wait."

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:48.900
And so I look back at the director,

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:51.110
I'm like, "I'm fine."
- I'm fine. (laughs)

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:53.360
- And then the door closes
and the emblem's right there.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:55.600
And I was like, I'm flipping out.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.730
Like I'm such a hip Prince fan.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:59.665
- Everyone is, I would
be sweating so much.

00:00:59.665 --> 00:01:01.140
- When I tell you,
- You just figured that out

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:02.000
right before you met him.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.590
- I did not know what to do with myself.

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:04.423
- Oh no.

00:01:04.423 --> 00:01:05.830
- So then he comes out of the hallway

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:07.150
and she's like, "Prince Megan's here."

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:08.850
And I'm like, "What?"

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:09.900
So he comes around the hallway,

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.390
He has these little Chinese pajamas

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:12.880
and he has on like these three chills

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:14.080
and his hair is tied up.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:15.900
He's got his powder and his eyeliner.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:17.750
And he was like, "Would
you like something to eat?"

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:19.710
And I was like, "Yes, yes."

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:20.700
Mind you I had just eaten.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.090
And so we go, we sit down,

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:24.780
and we're sitting at the table

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:26.510
and he's like, "Do you want salad?"

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:27.900
And I was like, "I would love salad."

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:29.600
I hate salad, now I'm better.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:31.240
- I love salad though.
- Now I do.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.660
But back then I was like, "Yes."

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:33.493
And then he was like, "Okay."

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:34.326
And then the person was like,

00:01:34.326 --> 00:01:35.237
"Well do you want salad Prince?"

00:01:35.237 --> 00:01:36.070
And he was like, "No."

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:37.420
I was like, "I don't want it either."

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:39.320
And then it just sounded
like I was like copying him.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:40.153
I was like, "No, but I really don't.

00:01:40.153 --> 00:01:41.770
I don't really eat salad that much.

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:42.603
It's okay."
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:42.603 --> 00:01:44.730
And then if they brought out wine

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:47.440
and literally as the woman's
walking back in the kitchen

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:48.803
Prince is like, (clears throat)

00:01:48.803 --> 00:01:50.210
and she's like, "Oh, I'm sorry. I forgot."

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:53.960
She comes back out with
a bright green straw

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:56.150
like a child's straw and
folds it over for him

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:57.730
and puts it in his red wine.

00:01:57.730 --> 00:01:59.100
And I was just like, okay.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.040
And I'm just watching like everything

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:02.990
and like the table's long
and he's at the head of it

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:04.490
and me and the director at the other side.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:06.600
And I looked down and I can see his feet

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.940
are about this far from the ground.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:10.060
And I can see him kind of going like that.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:11.740
And then like, he was
like making little shapes

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:13.420
on the table was the awkwardest dinner.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:16.500
And I had no idea why I was
there and what was going on.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:18.197
And then by the end of it, he was like,

00:02:18.197 --> 00:02:20.570
"I wanna make this documentary
about a young Malcolm X,

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:21.750
and I want you to play the character

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:23.020
and I wanna show it to you."

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:24.410
And I was like, "Oh, okay."

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.010
So then we watched a little
bit of documentary then I left

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:29.140
and then I pulled down the
street and I called my mom.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:30.995
I was like, "Mommy!"

00:02:30.995 --> 00:02:31.828
And like screaming.

00:02:31.828 --> 00:02:33.520
And then I like, literally, I
was like, "Can you hear me?"

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.430
And she's like, "What happened?

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:35.530
Did you get in a car accident?

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:36.772
I can't understand you."

00:02:36.772 --> 00:02:37.605
- Oh no.
(audience laughing)

00:02:37.605 --> 00:02:38.740
- And I was like, "No,
I'm trying to say that.

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:39.830
I just met Prince."

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:42.290
And so yeah, best, best day ever.

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:47.290
- Can I-
(audience clapping)

00:02:47.326 --> 00:02:50.560
- Can I tell you that
I'm actually still back

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:53.230
where he asked for bright green straw?

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.063
It's wine.

00:02:54.063 --> 00:02:56.020
- Yeah, I was like,
maybe he's a germophobe.

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:58.230
I don't know, I was
trying to put it together.

00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.930
- Oh gosh, that's amazing.

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:02.520
I'm like so weird, I wouldn't
have been able to let that go.

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:03.707
The whole dinner I'd have been like,

00:03:03.707 --> 00:03:05.070
"Why?"
- Not really?

00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:06.980
- I probably would've
had to have asked him.

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:08.470
That's why I've never met Prince.

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:12.060
He knew, he knew, don't invite
that weirdo to my house.

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:12.893
Have you ever met Prince?

00:03:12.893 --> 00:03:13.726
Did you ever meet him?

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:14.610
- No.
- Okay.

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:16.330
Yeah, we don't have cool stories.

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:17.470
Yeah. I'm not cool either.

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:20.850
It's like, everyone has one, it's crazy.

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:21.810
- Oh, I have a Prince story,

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:22.920
but it doesn't involve meeting him.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.060
- Oh wait, I wanna know the Prince story.

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:25.100
- You remember those little records,

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.211
they were like 33 and a
thirds back in the day.

00:03:27.211 --> 00:03:29.660
So they used to give those
out at bar mitzvah parties,

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:31.720
like if you won the limbo contest.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:33.150
I was 10 years old.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:35.810
It was my older brother's
friend's bar mitzvah.

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:39.110
And that was the prize
was "Erotic City" on 33.

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:40.730
Now, if you listen to "Erotic",

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:41.563
- [Kelly] What?

00:03:41.563 --> 00:03:43.511
- not appropriate for a 10-year-old.

00:03:43.511 --> 00:03:44.344
(audience laugh)

00:03:44.344 --> 00:03:45.323
It's my Prince story.

00:03:46.571 --> 00:03:49.546
- I love that they gave that out.

00:03:49.546 --> 00:03:52.089
- That is really wild.
(audience clapping)

00:03:52.089 --> 00:03:52.922
- Y'all know how to party, insane.

00:03:52.922 --> 00:03:55.251
- I wasn't really the limbo person.

00:03:55.251 --> 00:03:56.790
(all laughing)

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:58.820
- Limbo and some Prince, I love it.

